usage: poc [option]... <file>       build a program from <file>'s module
       poc [option]... <command>
an argument @<file> stands for the arguments in <file>, one a line,
and @@<text> for @<text>;
on VMS poc itself expands a file name's wildcards, * and %

commands:
  -build <file>              build a program, as poc <file> does
  -build <file> <t>.cld...   for vax-dec-vms: and link command tables
  -build <file> <o>.obj...   for vax-dec-vms: and link VAX object files
  -build <file> <f>.opt...   for vax-dec-vms: and add the options files' lines
  -build <file> <o>.o...     and link object files, each with no .sym beside it
  -check <file>              check a module, writing nothing
  -compile <file>...         compile modules to .sym, .ll and .o, not linked
  -library <name> <file>...  build the library <name> of the modules
                             (and object files, .o with no .sym beside it)
                             (for vax-dec-vms: and VAX object files, .obj,
                             and options files, .opt, whose lines -link's are)
  -install-library <name>    install the library <name> from the library path
  -emit-interface <file>     write the module's interface, <Module>.sym
  -show-interface <file>     print the module's interface
  -emit-llvm-ir <file>       write the module's LLVM IR, <Module>.ll
  -emit-macro32 <file>       write the module's VAX MACRO-32, <Module>.mar
  -print-import-path         print the import path, a directory a line
  -print-library-path        print the library path, a directory a line
  -version                   print poc's version, the target and clang's
  -help, -h, --help          print this

options, before or after the command (the last one counts, except those that add):
  -o <exe>                   the executable (default: the module's name)
  -output-dir <dir>          write .sym, .ll, .o files and libraries in <dir>
  -import-path <dir>         add <dir> to the import path
  -clear-import-path         forget the import path so far
  -library-path <dir>        add <dir> to the library path
  -clear-library-path        forget the library path so far, poc's own too
  -O2 | -OC                  size model: INTEGER 16/32 bits, LONGINT 32/64
  -strict                    only the Oberon-2 report: no extensions
  -g                         debug information: gdb, lldb, the VMS debugger
  -opt <level>               clang's -O: 0-3 s z g (default 2, 0 on 32-bit x86)
  -lto                       optimize the whole program when it is linked
  -rebuild                   compile every module, reusing no object
  -trap-location             a trap's message names its file, line, procedure
  -trap-heap-exhausted       a NEW that finds no memory stops the program
  -range-checks              SHORT and CHR of a value that does not fit trap
  -static                    link a fully static executable
  -shared-libraries          link libraries dynamically
  -vax-objects               for vax-dec-vms: build from poc's objects (on VMS)
  -vax-macro32               for vax-dec-vms: build from MACRO-32 (elsewhere)
  -link <arg>                add <arg> to the link (-lz, -L<dir>)
  -link <line>               for vax-dec-vms: add <line> to the link's options file
  -c-flag <arg>              add <arg> to clang's flags for a module's C part
  -target <triple>           compile for another target (vax-dec-vms: the VAX)
  -verbose                   print the commands poc runs

environment:
  POC_IMPORT_PATH            the import path to start from (dir:dir:...)
  POC$IMPORT                 on VMS, the import path to start from
  POC_LIBRARY_PATH           library path after -library-path (dir:dir:...)
  POC$LIBRARY                on VMS, the library path after -library-path

for testing poc itself:
  -dump-tokens <file>        print the module's tokens
  -check-syntax <file>       parse the module only
  -dump-layout <file>        print the memory layout of its records
  -dump-llvm-types <file>    print the LLVM type of each of its types
  -dump-nested <file>        print what its nested procedures need
  -dump-vax-types <file>     print the VAX size and suffix of each of its types
  -dump-vax-names <file>     print the VAX symbol of each of its names
  -emit-vax-image <file>     write each module encoded, <Module>.image
  -emit-vax-object <file>    write each module's VAX object, <Module>.obj

poc(1) explains each of them.
exit=1
